            Recomposition is possible for lean, well-trained lifters too, but it is slow, and progress can be hard to see. For that group, a planned muscle-gain phase in a small surplus followed by a fat-loss phase is often more efficient. If you are already lean and have trained hard for years, expect months of patience rather than weeks, and keep protein at the higher end of the range below. Our <a href="/best-protein-powder-for-beginners/">best protein powder for beginners</a> guide is a good place to start if you are new.
